    "stack": ["IntersectionObserver", "CSS transitions", "Emotion @keyframes (spinners only)"],
    "reduced_motion": "respected"
  },
  "notes": "Grafana uses Emotion (no CSS custom properties exposed — architecture.tokens.count=0), so tokens are inferred from computed styles + concatenated CSS. Colors are a single desaturated slate ramp; the one foreground #ccccdc is expressed at 1/0.65/0.3 alpha for the three text tiers (recorded as fg/muted/subtle). Type scale is compressed (~2x range, 14px body → 28px H1); '1.75rem' is that 28px H1. Roboto Mono is used for numeric/value readouts. Radius: 6px dominates chrome, 10px on media/blog cards. The 28 keyframes are Emotion-hashed spinner/slider animations, not scroll choreography — excluded from techniques."
}
